# SWR

- Always handle `isLoading` and `error` — never assume data is ready
- Fetchers live in `shared/api/`

```tsx
const { data, isLoading, error } = useSWR<UserModel>("/api/user", fetcher);

if (isLoading) return <Loader />;
if (error) return <ErrorMessage />;
```

# Errors

- Next.js App Router: use `error.tsx` Error Boundaries for render errors
- Async / event handlers: `try/catch`, surface errors to the user — do not swallow
- Always handle SWR `error` in the component
